WEBVTT

00:45:25.861 --> 00:45:31.057
and prepare for this future world
in which the routine jobs are displaced.

00:45:31.685 --> 00:45:33.946
CA: I'd love to just
dig into this a bit deeper,

00:45:33.970 --> 00:45:36.653
because in your talk and in your book,

00:45:36.677 --> 00:45:39.077
I think you have a very
distinctive way of thinking

00:45:39.101 --> 00:45:40.410
about the opportunity here,

00:45:40.434 --> 00:45:44.363
that I personally found quite inspiring
and super insightful.

00:45:44.680 --> 00:45:48.237
It was brought on by your own
brush with death or fears,

00:45:48.261 --> 00:45:51.950
you had a stage-four cancer diagnosis.

00:45:51.974 --> 00:45:55.922
And you were forced to rethink
your own values.

00:45:55.946 --> 00:46:00.067
And one particular insight
came out of that